        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(acp): close shared state database on gateway shutdown (#100637)",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes #100637: The standalone ACP gateway process (`serveAcpGateway`) opens a SQLite `DatabaseSync` connection through `createSqliteAcpEventLedger()` but never closes it on SIGINT/SIGTERM shutdown. This leaks file descriptors and causes SQLite file locking issues during hot reload.\n\nAdditionally, the original fix had an unbounded `Promise.allSettled` drain that could stall shutdown indefinitely if an ACP event handler never settled. This revision bounds the drain with a 2s timeout (matching the gateway shutdown pattern).\n\n## Changes\n\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `src/acp/server.ts` | Import `closeOpenClawStateDatabase`; track in-flight `handleGatewayEvent` promises; drain bounded by `ACP_SHUTDOWN_EVENT_DRAIN_TIMEOUT_MS` (2s) via `Promise.race`; close shared state DB after drain; call `onClosed()` after cleanup |\n| `src/acp/server.startup.test.ts` | 3 new tests: DB close on shutdown, bounded drain ordering, stalled-handler timeout (15 tests total) |\n| `src/acp/server.shutdown-proof.test.ts` | **Real-behavior proof**: uses real `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync` handles (no mocks) to prove `closeOpenClawStateDatabase` releases the underlying handle |\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit + proof tests (46/46 pass)\n\n```\n=== server.startup.test.ts (unit + drain regression) ===\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  15 passed (15)\n\n=== server.shutdown-proof.test.ts (real DatabaseSync proof) ===\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  1 passed (1)\n\n=== event-ledger.test.ts ===\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  12 passed (12)\n\n=== openclaw-state-db.test.ts ===\n Test Files  1 passed (1)\n      Tests  18 passed (18)\n```\n\n### Real-behavior proof detail\n\n`server.shutdown-proof.test.ts` exercises the shared state DB lifecycle with **real `node:sqlite` `DatabaseSync` instances** — the exact same API that the ACP event ledger uses internally. The test:\n\n1. Opens the shared state DB through `openOpenClawStateDatabase` (same path `createSqliteAcpEventLedger` takes)\n2. Asserts `db.isOpen === true` and `isOpenClawStateDatabaseOpen() === true`\n3. Calls `closeOpenClawStateDatabase` — the core of the ACP shutdown fix\n4. Asserts `db.isOpen === false` (proves the underlying `DatabaseSync` handle was actually closed, not just dropped from the module cache)\n5. Asserts `isOpenClawStateDatabaseOpen() === false` (proves no cached handle remains)\n\n### Drain timeout regression test detail\n\n`server.startup.test.ts` \"continues shutdown after the event drain timeout when a handler stalls\":\n\n1. Creates a handler that never settles (simulated stalled `sessionUpdate`)\n2. Fires a gateway event → handler begins, tracked in `inFlightEvents`\n3. Triggers SIGINT shutdown → hits `Promise.race([allSettled, timeout])`\n4. Advances fake timers past 2s → timeout wins\n5. Verifies `closeOpenClawStateDatabase` was called (shutdown completed despite stalled handler)\n\n### Diff scope\n\n```\n src/acp/server.shutdown-proof.test.ts | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/acp/server.startup.test.ts        | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n src/acp/server.ts                     | 18 +++++++++++--\n 3 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>",
